 These restrictions leave concrete lessons for representation analysis. Report the action class and metric when claiming compatibility; separate a constructed predictor's transfer from the class optimum; compare coherent alternatives with their target definitions and absolute margins; and inspect domain and condition variation before interpreting an aggregate. Stable state coding remains compatible with the observed structure, and the unsuccessful clean-competence checks prevent a native-computation conclusion from the historical intervention branch. The full theoretical assumptions, unfavorable outcomes, historical controls and reproducibility records remain in the appendices and supplement. They delimit a finite-bank analysis, not a calibrated population-level identification procedure.
 
